# Kept in sync with .gitignore's intent, plus Docker-specific excludes.
# `turbo prune --docker` (used by apps/web/Dockerfile and
# apps/simulation-worker/Dockerfile) copies the whole build context
# into its own stage first — without this, that copy drags along every
# workspace's node_modules/.next/.turbo output, which is enormous and
# also stale (the build stages install/build fresh inside the image).
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a bare `pattern` in .dockerignore only matches at
# the build context ROOT — it does NOT recurse into subdirectories the
# way gitignore's does. Every pattern below needs an explicit `**/`
# prefix to match inside apps/*/packages/* — a bug caught here by
# actually running `docker build` and finding a stale
# tsconfig.tsbuildinfo (bare `*.tsbuildinfo` didn't match
# packages/database/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo) making `tsc --build` believe
# a fresh checkout was already compiled and silently emit nothing.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env
**/.env.local
.git
**/.DS_Store
